<p>The Trump administration said it may soon remove sanctions on about 140 million barrels of Iranian oil already stranded on tankers at sea, a step Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said could add supply and help bring down prices as Washington tries to curb soaring oil costs. Bessent said the move could affect prices over the next 10 to 14 days, underscoring the administration&#x27;s push to ease pressure in energy markets. The proposal highlights a practical split in Washington&#x27;s approach: keeping pressure on Tehran while also trying to prevent a prolonged oil-price shock for consumers and the broader global economy. Reports also said officials are weighing other options, including another release from the Strategic Petroleum Reserve, while ruling out restrictions on US oil and gas exports during internal discussions with industry leaders.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/NUOPuBgr9k4Ut3FLtRuASmQwYHdXyCvH0-seRy-RiR_-IW33JPGW9JpOs56W7zBlzKn88FMefDFzpjoS1FXrYsJt-Elst5qdCCKccJGZJticOhOFR4InbnW-LxsOLqgasZGRo8-uqXAU6uM9yYKOl0UsJjz4fe6QDs1x_s7O8SchEfEo8jR8BuTApAcSjJtH5DOT9kpxjXmAyvhtJIh0fCDbLu1JFGqBHdNQgeRqjNJHOG8AdHRbOT5IcD2bfck0POIoWCvktxJ4V0kCYw' alt='US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent arrives to give a press statement at the OECD Headquarters, Monday, March 16, 2026, in Paris, France. (AP Photo/Emma Da Silva)' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Price spike: Oil climbed above $119 a barrel early Thursday, adding urgency to the administration&#x27;s search for extra supply.</li><li>Supply window: Bessent said releasing the oil already at sea would help keep prices down for roughly the next 10 to 14 days.</li><li>Other levers: Bessent also floated another Strategic Petroleum Reserve release as one of the administration&#x27;s policy options.</li><li>Exports spared: At a meeting with oil executives and Vice President JD Vance, officials ruled out curbs on US oil and gas exports, which experts said could raise costs rather than lower them.</li></ul><blockquote>In the coming days, we may un-sanction the Iranian oil that’s on the water. It’s about 140m barrels. - Scott Bessent</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent: Bessent framed the possible sanctions relief as a short-term market intervention meant to add immediate supply and ease the oil-price surge. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/19/us-sanctions-iranian-oil-hormuz'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Trump administration officials: Officials signaled they preferred supply-side responses such as unsanctioning oil or tapping the petroleum reserve rather than limiting US exports, which they saw as counterproductive. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/19/2026/treasury-eyes-lifting-sanctions-on-iranian-oil'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump told reporters the oil-price news was manageable, saying he had expected worse numbers. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/19/2026/treasury-eyes-lifting-sanctions-on-iranian-oil'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/us/politics/iran-oil-sanctions.html'>U.S. Encourages Flow of Iranian Oil While It Battles Iran</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/19/us-sanctions-iranian-oil-hormuz'>US may remove sanctions on Iranian oil stranded in tankers, treasury secretary says</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/19/2026/treasury-eyes-lifting-sanctions-on-iranian-oil'>Treasury eyes lifting sanctions on Iranian oil</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-us-sanctions-iran-oil-bessent/'>U.S. may remove sanctions on Iranian oil stranded at sea, Bessent says</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-may-remove-sanctions-on-iranian-oil-stranded-in-tankers-bessent-says/article70764058.ece'>U.S. may remove sanctions on Iranian oil stranded in tankers, Bessent says</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>